Module 7: Reporting and Analytics
We are onto the final major functionality module! A robust POS system isn't just about taking money; it's about providing the business owners with clear, actionable insights into how the store is performing.

Based on your design document, Module 7 will provide: Daily/Monthly sales reports, Best-selling products tracking, and Inventory valuation.

Proposed Execution Plan
Phase 1: Database Layer (No Schema Changes!)
The best part of Module 7 is that it proves our database from Modules 1-6 was designed perfectly! We do not need to create any new tables. Instead, we will write complex SQL Aggregation Queries (using SUM(), GROUP BY, and DATE() math) to extract analytics natively from our existing tables.

Phase 2: Backend API Upgrades
[NEW] server/routes/reports.js
I will create three primary reporting endpoints. These will be strictly guarded by our authorizeRoles('Administrator', 'Manager') middleware so Cashiers cannot see the store's daily revenues!

Sales Summary Report: Returns total revenue calculated for "Today", "This Week", and "This Month".
Top Products Report: Joins sales_items with products to find which items were mathematically bought the most often.
Inventory Valuation: Calculates the total raw dollar value sitting in the store's warehouse (SUM(quantity * price)).
